          <!-- BODY -->
          <tr>
            <td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:28px 32px;
                       font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#212121;">

              <p>Hello fellow hams,</p>

              <p>
                The second hunt of the 2026 season is coming up in
                two weeks. Join us for an on-foot ARDF hunt at
                <strong>Marymoor Park</strong> in Redmond &mdash;
                640 acres of wooded Sammamish River corridor and
                open fields that offer a more challenging hunting
                environment than July&rsquo;s practice event.
              </p>

              <p>
                Marymoor is accessible by light rail (2 Line,
                Marymoor Village Station) as well as by car.
                Mentors will be present, and loaner equipment is
                available for those without their own gear.
              </p>

              <p style="background-color:#fff8e1;border-left:4px solid
                        #f0a500;padding:12px 16px;margin:16px 0;
                        font-size:14px;">
                <strong>Note:</strong> We must wrap up by
                <strong>2:30&nbsp;PM</strong>. Marymoor Live
                concerts begin setup at 4&nbsp;PM and the park
                becomes very crowded by mid-afternoon.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                Event Details
              </h3>
              <table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0"
                     border="0"
                     style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.9;">
                <tr>
                  <td width="140"
                      style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Date &amp; Time:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>Saturday, August 22, 2026</strong>,
                    Noon &ndash; 2:30&nbsp;PM
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Location:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>Marymoor Park</strong><br>
                    6046 W Lake Sammamish Pkwy NE,
                    Redmond, WA&nbsp;98052
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Frequency:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    <strong>147.42&nbsp;MHz simplex</strong>
                    (callsign K7LED); net control on K7LED repeater
                    (alt 146.580&nbsp;MHz FM simplex)
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Parking:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    Paid parking may apply. See King County parking
                    passes/rates page for current fees; arrive
                    before noon to secure a spot before concert
                    traffic builds.
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Transit:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    Sound Transit 2 Line &mdash; Marymoor
                    Village Station (0.4&nbsp;mi walk to park)
                  </td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td style="color:#555555;vertical-align:top;">
                    Hunt type:
                  </td>
                  <td style="vertical-align:top;">
                    Single milliwatt fox, on-foot ARDF
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                What to Bring
              </h3>
              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Handheld transceiver</strong> programmed
                  to 147.42&nbsp;MHz &mdash; or borrow one at
                  the event
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Tape-measure Yagi antenna</strong>
                  &mdash; or borrow one at the event
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Switched step attenuator (for close-in work)
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Comfortable walking shoes; mixed trail and
                  open-field terrain
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Water and a snack; sun protection for the
                  open sections
                </li>
              </ul>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                RSVP &amp; Questions
              </h3>
              <p>
                An RSVP helps us plan loaner radios. Reply to
                this message or contact
                <strong>Tom Sayles, KE4HET</strong> at
                <a href="mailto:TSayles@Soot-n-Smoke.com">TSayles@Soot-n-Smoke.com</a>.
              </p>
              <p>
                Participation is open (no registration required). Check
                in with net control at hunt start or when you begin
                hunting.
              </p>

              <p>
                We look forward to seeing you at Marymoor. 73
                de KE4HET
              </p>

